         'These quarrels have made our nation very weak and broken it into pieces. The blessing of unity has left our nation. This worthless disunity has done great harm to national sympathy, national progress and the carrying out of national affairs. So the very first stage of our national progress is that, through mutual love, we all replace this enmity and discord with oneness and unity.',
